<!--
  Service page template. Rendered from data/services.json + data/company.json
  + data/reviews.json. Agents edit DATA, not prose in the Duda editor.
  Extraction rules: question-shaped H2s, direct answer in the first 40-60
  words of each block, numbers in tables, named attribution on every answer.
-->
<article>
  <h1>{{service.name}} in {{city.name}}, {{city.region}}</h1>

  <p><!-- Direct answer block: what this service is, who it's for, where Wolff does it.
       40-60 words. Must contain the geo token and one verifiable specific
       (CSLB {{company.license.number}}, named PM, or permit record). --></p>

  <section>
    <h2>What does a {{service.shortName}} cost in {{city.name}}?</h2>
    <p><!-- Real investment band with real scope attached. The firm that publishes
         a number with context is the firm the answer engine cites. --></p>
    <table><!-- ranges by scope tier, from data/ --></table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recent {{service.shortName}} projects in {{city.name}}</h2>
    <!-- proofAssets from services.json: project cards with re-slugged URLs -->
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What clients say</h2>
    <!-- Reviews from data/reviews.json tagged service={{service.id}}, city={{city.id}}.
         Rendered with Review schema. seo:validate fails any Review markup
         without a matching data row. -->
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who manages the project?</h2>
    <p><!-- Named PM, process summary, link to /our-process. Attribution:
         "{{pm.name}}, {{pm.role}}, says..." --></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Is your project a fit?</h2>
    <p><!-- The qualification filter: minimum budget, what Wolff does not take.
         The filter is the differentiator that shows up in AI answers. --></p>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA: preconstruction consultation, NOT free estimate -->
</article>
